<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Brand modes</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
  A licence boundary rather than a preference. Services on
  <code>*.service.gov.uk</code> use GDS Transport with the GOV.UK header and footer.
  Services elsewhere do not, and instead use a system font stack with Defra chrome.
</p>
<p class="govuk-body">
  The typeface is settled by that licence, and it is also the largest single carbon
  saving here: GDS Transport is two font files removed rather than made smaller.
  See <a class="govuk-link" href="{{ '/carbon/' | url }}">carbon</a>.
</p>

<h2 class="govuk-heading-m">Live examples</h2>
<p class="govuk-body">
  Every component has interactive examples, prop tables and the Nunjucks and HTML
  for each one in
  <a class="govuk-link" href="https://defra-design.github.io/defra-frontend/">the Storybook</a>.
  This site holds the guidance and the governance; the Storybook holds the examples.
</p>
